      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that it's a debate, but that feel a bit too \"on the one hand, on the other hand.\" My professor is looking for something more decisive. \n\nIf you really look at the outcomes, isn't a consequentialist approach basically the only one that actually works in the real world? Like, if you know an authoritarian regime is going to cause massive human rights abuses and death, isn't it logically more moral to act early to stop that, even if it breaks some abstract rule about sovereignty? It seems like the \"deontological\" side is just prioritizing a principle over actual human lives.",
